{"type":"message","id":"8f8b8b26","parentId":"8b8a5e4d","timestamp":"2026-05-25T09:42:25.297Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"exec_ts_ZTI0ODMwYTctNWNkNi00MmZlLTk5OGItZWU1MzllNzJiOWMz","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Let's extract the article on Vitalik Buterin from Cointelegraph using trafilatura\ntrafilatura -u \"https://cointelegraph.com/news/buterin-fires-back-ef-critics-neutrality?utm_source=rss_feed&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=rss_partner_inbound\" --output-format markdown\n"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"local-bifrost","model":"gemini-3.5-flash","usage":{"input":50073,"output":96,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":50169,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779702142982,"responseId":"gRkUasquDtfs694PvMzu2Ao"}}
{"type":"message","id":"788dcc16","parentId":"8f8b8b26","timestamp":"2026-05-25T09:42:25.994Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"exec_ts_ZTI0ODMwYTctNWNkNi00MmZlLTk5OGItZWU1MzllNzJiOWMz","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"*The Ethereum Foundation's mandate was published in March 2026. Source: **Ethereum Foundation*\n\n“Now, we are taking action to ensure that we will be the latter,” he continued, adding that the Ethereum Foundation seeks to strengthen Ethereum’s cybersecurity and code base but not necessarily compete with high-throughput chains or scale to 1 million transactions per second.\n\nThe comments follow several large ETH holders selling their entire ETH position and high-profile departures from the Ethereum Foundation, as the current price of the cryptocurrency, about $2,094, sits more than 50% below its all-time high of nearly $5,000 reached in August 2025.\n\n“The EF has only about 0.16% of all ETH,” he said, noting that it is common for other foundations to hold 10-50% of their native tokens.\n\n**Related: ****Blockchain researcher defends Ethereum Foundation, says it’s doing ‘exactly’ its job**\n\n“I think Ethereum’s original sin was not considering tokenomics with every move it made from Dencun on,” cryptocurrency journalist Laura Shin said.\n\nThe Dencun upgrade was a major protocol update released in March 2024, which significantly reduced network fees for layer-2 transactions and led to a subsequent collapse in Ethereum’s base layer revenue.\n\n*Fees on the Ethereum layer-1 blockchain network fell significantly after the Dencun upgrade in March 2024. Source: **Token Terminal*\n\nMost investors “don’t want to believe in something that is not also putting up points on the scoreboard,” Shin said about ETH.\n\nButerin said on Sunday that the Foundation would focus on “longevity” and stretch its funds to finance research, meaning it would sell less ETH in the future.\n\nIn May, the Foundation unstaked 21,270 ETH from the Lido liquid staking platform, as part of its treasury strategy.\n\nUnstaking ETH means those holdings will no longer generate yield for the Ethereum Foundation, but it is not a confirmation that the organization will sell those tokens.\n\n**Magazine: ****Why is Ethereum Foundation selling? BTC futures warning signs: Market Moves**\n\nMore on the subject"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":659,"aggregated":"*The Ethereum Foundation's mandate was published in March 2026. Source: **Ethereum Foundation*\n\n“Now, we are taking action to ensure that we will be the latter,” he continued, adding that the Ethereum Foundation seeks to strengthen Ethereum’s cybersecurity and code base but not necessarily compete with high-throughput chains or scale to 1 million transactions per second.\n\nThe comments follow several large ETH holders selling their entire ETH position and high-profile departures from the Ethereum Foundation, as the current price of the cryptocurrency, about $2,094, sits more than 50% below its all-time high of nearly $5,000 reached in August 2025.\n\n“The EF has only about 0.16% of all ETH,” he said, noting that it is common for other foundations to hold 10-50% of their native tokens.\n\n**Related: ****Blockchain researcher defends Ethereum Foundation, says it’s doing ‘exactly’ its job**\n\n“I think Ethereum’s original sin was not considering tokenomics with every move it made from Dencun on,” cryptocurrency journalist Laura Shin said.\n\nThe Dencun upgrade was a major protocol update released in March 2024, which significantly reduced network fees for layer-2 transactions and led to a subsequent collapse in Ethereum’s base layer revenue.\n\n*Fees on the Ethereum layer-1 blockchain network fell significantly after the Dencun upgrade in March 2024. Source: **Token Terminal*\n\nMost investors “don’t want to believe in something that is not also putting up points on the scoreboard,” Shin said about ETH.\n\nButerin said on Sunday that the Foundation would focus on “longevity” and stretch its funds to finance research, meaning it would sell less ETH in the future.\n\nIn May, the Foundation unstaked 21,270 ETH from the Lido liquid staking platform, as part of its treasury strategy.\n\nUnstaking ETH means those holdings will no longer generate yield for the Ethereum Foundation, but it is not a confirmation that the organization will sell those tokens.\n\n**Magazine: ****Why is Ethereum Foundation selling? BTC futures warning signs: Market Moves**\n\nMore on the subject","cwd":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1779702145994}}
{"type":"message","id":"015bea77","parentId":"788dcc16","timestamp":"2026-05-25T09:42:29.910Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"exec_ts_ZTI0ODMwYTctNWNkNi00MmZlLTk5OGItZWU1MzllNzJiOWMz","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Let's check The Block's article on Vitalik Buterin and Ethereum Foundation:\n# Title: \"Vitalik Buterin says Ethereum Foundation will be a 'smaller ship,' sell less ETH amid researcher exodus\"\n# Let's find its URL or similar. Let's see if we can read the KuCoin / Cryptonews.net or Yahoo Finance / The Block article directly.\n# Let's search the Google News output for \"Vitalik Buterin says Ethereum Foundation will be a 'smaller ship'\"\n# Google News URL: https://news.google.?oc=5\n# Let's verify the google news redirect URL to get the direct URL to The Block if possible, or we can just fetch via trafilatura.\n# Let's see if we can use trafilatura on the google news URL directly:\ntrafilatura -u \"https://news.google.?oc=5\" --output-format markdown\n"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"local-bifrost","model":"gemini-3.5-flash","usage":{"input":2748,"output":621,"cacheRead":47885,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":51254,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779702145997,"responseId":"hBkUaq7QBq-H694P94bj4QQ"}}
